 2. Microsoft pulls plug on Oracle 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Microsoft is reportedly ending its arrangements to rent AI computing from Oracle.

 The news sent Oracle's stock down over 5 percentage points this afternoon before it clawed back into the green. It ended the day up 0.8%, Pete writes . Zoom in: The deal, in place since 2023, included computing capacity powered by older-generation Nvidia chips, which was becoming less useful for Microsoft, Bloomberg reported .

 It comes amid a larger effort from Microsoft to move away from compute deals with neocloud providers. Oracle posted a public statement on X this afternoon saying demand for its AI infrastructure "remains strong, including for earlier-generation GPUs."

 
 
